    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Longitudinal tensor-based morphometry study of older smokers (successful and unsuccessful quitters) vs never smokers (I1 met; original data, E2 not met). The only between-group imaging contrasts compare GM density change over 24 months. They were restricted by inclusive masks from each group's within-group loss maps, so the search was not whole-brain. No cross-sectional whole-brain comparison of GM volume between users and controls is reported. A qualifying whole-brain contrast was not demonstrated (I2 not met)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "21310189",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I1",
     "I2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Empirical MRI study of adolescent marijuana users vs controls, but it measures only cortical thickness (FreeSurfer vertex-wise), not GM volume, density or concentration. I1 not met. The only whole-brain group contrast is of cortical thickness; no whole-brain GM volume contrast is reported (I2 not met). Total brain volume is a global measure only. The ROI analysis supplements a whole-brain analysis (E1 not met). The paper is empirical (E2 not met)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "21909705",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I2",
     "E1"
    ],
    "autonima": "excluded_fulltext",
    "reason": "Empirical VBM study comparing GM volume in 33 smokers vs 22 never-smokers (I1 met). The analysis used the SUIT toolbox, which isolates the cerebellum and brainstem from the rest of the brain, so the GM contrast is restricted to infratentorial structures. No whole-brain between-group GM contrast is shown (I2 not met), and the only results come from a restricted region (E1 met). The paper reports original data (E2 not met)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "23149031",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
