    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Longitudinal tensor-based morphometry study comparing GM loss in cannabis users (n=23) vs non-users (n=32), all at familial high risk of schizophrenia (I1 met, E2 not met). A whole-brain contrast was run but reached no significance; three regions were described only in prose, with no coordinates or statistics. All reported results (Table 2 coordinates) come from small-volume corrections restricted to the hippocampus/amygdala, frontal lobes and thalami. So no qualifying whole-brain contrast is reported (I2 not met), and the results are effectively ROI-only (E1 met). The comparison group is also high-risk non-users rather than healthy controls."
   },
